cl folds or omits every symbol this case's classes would need - NP's implicit constructor and destructor, V's inline virtual, and the vftables of V and VD - where cxx1 emits real ones, so the diff is five lines from cxx1 with nothing answering from cl. Same reason base-tail-padding.nonames records against clang for this ABI, and the same one docs/CONFORMANCE.md gives under "An inline member function is a strong symbol". What this case measures is layout, and the layout is pinned by static_asserts that cl's own answers were measured for: sizeof(ND) 12 and sizeof(VD) 24 on this ABI where Itanium says 8 and 16
